e":"שלום יוסי, ברוך הבא!","en":"Hi Yossi, welcome!","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"תפוח או תפוז, בבקשה.","en":"An apple or an orange, please.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"שלום, קוראים לי יוסי.","en":"Hi, my name is Yossi.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אני רוצֶה אפרסק בבקשה.","en":"I want a peach please.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אני רוצֶה פסטה, בבקשה.","en":"I want pasta, please.","alt":[],"t":"t","inferred":1},{"he":"אני רוצָה אפרסק בבקשה.","en":"I want a peach please.","alt":[],"t":"l","inferred":1},{"he":"בוקר טוב, אני מדבר עברית!","en":"Good morning, I speak Hebrew!","alt":[],"t":"l"},{"he":"סליחה, אני לא מדבר עברית.","en":"Sorry, I don't speak Hebrew.","alt":[],"t":"t"}],"hints":{"אולי":"maybe, perhaps","בסדר":"alright / fine / ok","עברית":"Hebrew","שלום":"hello / hi / peace","תודה":"thank you / thanks","אנגלית":"english","בבקשה":"here you go / please / you are welcome","בהצלחה":"good luck","סליחה":"I am sorry / pardon / excuse me","לא":"aren't / didn't / do not","להתראות":"goodbye","מה":"everything / nothing can be done / there is nothing to do","נשמע":"sound / sounded / sounds","קורה":"what is happening / what's happening / what's up","ערב":"evening","טוב":"alright / good / ok","בתיאבון":"bon appetit","אני":"I / I am / I am a girl","אתה":"you / you are / you (masculine singular)","הבא":"next","כן":"yes","תהני":"have fun! (feminine singular)","בוקר":"breakfast / breakfasts / for breakfast","יפֶה":"beautiful / beautiful (feminine singular) / handsome","אין":"not has / not have / nothing can be done","הבאה":"next / the next (feminine singular) / next, nearest, coming (masculine singular)","מזל":"luck / congratulations","תהנו":"have fun! (masculine singular)","או":"or","לילה":"night","אבא":"dad / father / father, dad","אמא":"mom / mother / mum","בקרוב":"soon, shortly","מדבר":"speak / speaks / talks","את":"it / that / the fruit","קוראים":"read (masculine plural)","לי":"I have / for me / me","חותם":"sign, seal, finish","תפוח":"an apple / apple","תפוז":"an orange / orange / orange (fruit)","רוצֶה":"want / wants / would like","אפרסק":"a peach / peach","פסטה":"pasta","רוצָה":"want / wants / would like"},"words":[{"he":"מה","en":"what","alt":["everything","nothing can be done","there is nothing to do","what are","what do","what does","what is"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"mah"},{"he":"תודה","en":"thanks","alt":["thank you"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"todah"},{"he":"טוב","en":"good","alt":["alright","ok","well"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"tov"},{"he":"שלום","en":"hi","alt":["hello","peace"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"shalom"},{"he":"בסדר","en":"fine","alt":["alright","ok"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"b'seder"},{"he":"קורה","en":"what's up","alt":["what is happening","what's happening"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"ערב","en":"evening","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"erev"},{"he":"עברית","en":"Hebrew","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"ivrit"},{"he":"סליחה","en":"sorry","alt":["I am sorry","pardon","excuse me"],"from":"skill","tr":"s'likhah"},{"he":"בבקשה","en":"please","alt":["here you go","you are welcome"],"from":"skill","tr":"b'vakashah"},{"he":"אין בעד מה","en":"you are welcome","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"ein"},{"he":"מה קורה","en":"what's happening?, what's up?","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"mah"},{"he":"בתיאבון","en":"bon appetit","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"b'te'avon"},{"he":"תודה רבה","en":"thankyou very much","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"todah"},{"he":"בהצלחה","en":"good luck","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"b'hatzlakhah"},{"he":"מזל טוב","en":"congratulations","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"mazal"},{"he":"מה נשמע","en":"how are you?","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"mah"},{"he":"אנגלית","en":"english","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"ang'lit"},{"he":"להתראות","en":"goodbye","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"l'hit'raot"},{"he":"מה שלומךְ","en":"how are you? (feminine)","alt":["how are you? (masculine)"],"from":"skill","tr":"mah"}],"lexemes":["עברית","סליחה","בבקשה","שלום","אין בעד מה","תודה","מה קורה","בתיאבון","בסדר","תודה רבה","בהצלחה","מזל טוב","טל","מה נשמע","אנגלית","להתראות","יוסי","מה שלומךְ"],"tips":"NEW USERS AND PEOPLE NEW TO HEBREW: See [here](https://duolinguists.wordpress.com/typing-in-hebrew-learning-alef-bet-for-beginners/) for quick instructions on **typing** and **learning to read** Hebrew.\n\nWelcome\n------------\n\nThe word \"welcome\" has 4 versions:\n\n* **ברוך הבא** (barúkh habá) - for singular masculine.\n\n* **ברוכה הבאה** (brukhá haba'á) - for singular feminine.\n\n* **ברוכים הבאים** (brukhím haba'ím) - for plural masculine/mixed (and when no one in particular is being addressed, for example on a place sign).\n\n* **ברוכות הבאות** (brukhót haba'ót) - for plural feminine.\n\n----------\nNames\n----------\n\nIn this lesson we introduce two common Israeli names:\n\nיוסי (Yossi) - Male name (shortened from the equivalent of \"Joseph\", Yosef - יוסף)\n\nטל (Tal) - Unisex name (meaning \"dew\")\n\n-----------\nHow are you?\n-----------\n\nAs in English, there are various ways to ask someone how they are, or what's going on. Here we introduce the following:\n\n?מה קורה  \nLiterally: \"What's happening?\" Similar to \"What's up?\", \"How are you doing?\"\n\n?מה נשמע  \nLiterally: \"What is heard?\" Used in the same way as מה קורה.\n\n?מה שלומך  \n(when addressing a male: מה שלומךָ (ma shlomkhá), when addressing a female: מה שלומךְ (ma shlomékh))  \nLiterally this means \"what is your peace/well-being/welfare?\". This is the standard, formal way of asking \"how are you?\".\n\n--------------\nCongratulations and good luck!\n--------------\n\nThe Hebrew phrase for \"congratulations\" is \"מזל טוב\" (maz**a**l tov) - not \"**ma**zel tov\" like in Yiddish!\nLiterally it means \"good luck\" but it isn't used to wish someone good luck, it simply means that they have already had some good luck (mazal = luck; tov = good).\n\nThe Hebrew phrase for \"good luck\" is בהצלחה (be'hatzlakha), literally \"in/with success\"."}